        new("python-background-work", "Production systems", 28, "Design durable background work", "A queue moves work; it does not remove failure modes.", "Idempotency, retries, visibility, and ownership make asynchronous work reliable.", "Use background jobs for durable, slow, or retryable work. Give each job a stable idempotency key, make handlers safe to retry, configure bounded retries and dead-letter handling, and measure age, failures, and throughput. Use an outbox or equivalent when an event must correspond to committed state.", "def send_completion_email(enrollment_id: str) -> None:\n    if delivery_log.exists(enrollment_id):\n        return\n    # send, then record delivery atomically where possible", new(ExerciseKind.MultipleChoice, "Make retries safe", "What makes a job safe to retry?", ["Choose one answer"], null, "idempotent", [new("idempotent", "Repeated processing does not create an unintended extra effect"), new("fast", "It completes in under one second"), new("async", "It is declared with `async def`")], "Retries are normal in distributed systems; effects must tolerate them.", ["Designs idempotent jobs"]), "python-performance-caching", PythonDocs),
